  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1)\n\nNorthwest flow aloft with an embedded disturbance dropping from the \nGreat Lakes thru the Ohio Valley. Associated surface cold front to\nsweep south thru the region this morning. Moderate instability \nahead of this front is supporting the development of clusters of\nthunderstorms. These storms may produce isolated strong wind gusts\nand small hail. As the night progresses these storms will become\nmore elevated and the threat for severe weather decreases.  \n\nA cold front will sweep southeast through our local area this morning\nand winds will shift to the northwesterly winds and low clouds  \nscattered out this afternoon. Temperatures look to be closer to\nnormal today with highs generally in the lower and middle 80s. \n\nHigh pressure will offer cooler and drier conditions thru most of the\nweek. Temperatures will be a bit below normal through at least \nThursday and potentially into Friday.",
